1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
A sound soul, dwells within a sound mind, and a sound body.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Welcome to Death Weapon Meister Academy.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:32,000
More commonly known as the DWMA.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:41,000
It stands as a defense against the forces of evil, which would plunge the world into chaos and drag humanity to the very depths of fear and madness.

5
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The demons known as Keishin, and their insatiable hunger for destruction.

6
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000
To ensure the Keishin never regain their hold on this world, this academy was founded by the Grim Reaper, Death himself.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
So basically, we're an organization that exists to protect and preserve peace.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
I guess it's not exactly a typical school.

9
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Oh well, that isn't important. For now, let's roll up our sleeves and get to work!

10
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:27,000
einem

11
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:37,000
魂の火が胸を刺すなら 言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

12
00:01:37,000 --> 00:02:00,300
六人目も合わさず 運命まで絡んでく 行き先もらったポテル 食えない夜の端で

13
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:09,660
不可愛しすぎた眩しさが 悪い夢に続いても

14
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:23,760
繋いだ魂の火が胸を刺すなら 言葉よりもっと強い響きが今聞こえるか

15
00:02:23,760 --> 00:02:34,760
やっと理由は途絶びに惹きつけられて 触れた瞬間の傷の分だけ確かになれる

16
00:02:34,760 --> 00:03:04,740
ご視聴ありがとうございました

17
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:34,740
ご視聴ありがとうございました

18
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:50,740
ご視聴ありがとうございました

19
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:53,680
Patty, your stances off again, the two of you aren't in a line.

20
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:55,000
Oh!

21
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,320
I'm sorry, kid.

22
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:01,740
Uh, kid, do you really think now is the time to be worrying about that?

23
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,120
Yes, I do.

24
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:04,960
I want it to be perfect every time.

25
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:07,460
I know, but do you think that this works, maybe?

26
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:13,040
How many times do I have to tell you everything must be in perfect balance?

27
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:15,420
Symmetry is what makes the world beautiful.

28
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,360
He ran away, he ran away!

29
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:18,620
Patty, why can't you be quiet and listen to what I'm talking?

30
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,820
Is that so much to ask, huh?

31
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:20,200
Okay.

32
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:23,920
Symmetry is key.

33
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:25,680
Everything must be aesthetically pleasing.

34
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:27,420
Oh, wonderful. Here we go.

35
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:31,660
That's why I use the two of you as twin pistols in order to preserve symmetry.

36
00:04:32,140 --> 00:04:34,880
When I hold you both, I'm completely balanced on the right and left.

37
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:38,480
It isn't perfect because your human forms are so different from each other, though.

38
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:40,740
Your hairstyles and height, for example.

39
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:44,680
Even your boobs are different sizes!

40
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,900
Excuse me for being smaller than my little sister!

41
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,480
What night do you have to talk about symmetry anyway?

42
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:54,240
Three stripes on the left side of your hair and none on the right?

43
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:56,280
That doesn't look symmetrical to me!

44
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,360
You're right! I'm an abomination!

45
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:02,060
I'm filthy and dirty and unbalanced!

46
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,700
Why is there only one set of stripes?

47
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:04,720
I'm garbage!

48
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,320
A symmetrical garbage!

49
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,700
I deserve to die!

50
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,440
Yeah, and here we go.

51
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,360
Patty?

52
00:05:13,740 --> 00:05:14,140
Yes!

53
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:18,080
Now, now, kid, you can't forget that you're a grim reaper.

54
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:20,460
Compared to that, what do three little lines matter?

55
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:21,860
Yeah, kid, you're not garbage!

56
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:23,980
If you were garbage, then you'd smell a lot worse!

57
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:25,780
So why don't we just get up and try again, okay?

58
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:29,740
You don't think I'm asymmetrical garbage, really?

59
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:31,920
No, of course not!

60
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,740
Garbage is ew, and you're not!

61
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,120
All right, then.

62
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:36,920
Let's report to my father.

63
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,480
Not the sharpest tool in the shed, is he?

64
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:41,540
These little rich kids are always so gullible.

65
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,660
Well, hello, son! What's up?

66
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,320
It's good to see you!

67
00:05:57,480 --> 00:06:00,140
I've forgotten how cute those stripes in your hair are!

68
00:06:00,660 --> 00:06:01,580
Stop it, Dad.

69
00:06:01,860 --> 00:06:03,100
I'm not a little kid anymore.

70
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:04,180
Is that really necessary?

71
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:07,000
That's a sensitive topic right now, sir!

72
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:07,820
Huh?

73
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:10,620
Okay, then. We'll just move along.

74
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:11,600
How are things going?

75
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:14,780
It looks like you're making some good progress collecting Kishan souls.

76
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:17,760
But, kid, don't forget, you're a grim reaper.

77
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:20,940
You don't really need to be training weapons or reclaiming souls.

78
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:25,240
Even so, I want to make my own weapons to my own specifications.

79
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,240
Huh.

80
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:28,520
In that case, since you have two weapons,

81
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:31,040
the number of souls you must collect is double the normal amount.

82
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:33,440
This means you'll have to work harder, too, Liz and Patty.

83
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,640
Yes, sir!

84
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:35,660
I understand.

85
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:38,620
And I would like to collect all of the souls that I need in one go.

86
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:41,380
So, do you have any suitable targets for me right now?

87
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,720
Ah, well, now that you mention it,

88
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,800
as a matter of fact, I do have one.

89
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,880
What's going on there?

90
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:54,640
Hey!

91
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:55,520
Soul!

92
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:56,040
Maka!

93
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:57,620
Oh, hey, guys. Good morning.

94
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:58,860
Morning, Maka.

95
00:06:59,220 --> 00:06:59,540
Soul.

96
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:02,000
What happened?

97
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,260
Why is everyone down here?

98
00:07:03,580 --> 00:07:03,980
Seriously?

99
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:05,280
You mean you haven't heard yet?

100
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:07,700
It's kind of a hot topic around here right now.

101
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:09,140
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

102
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,140
Oh, I get it.

103
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:12,580
Everyone's scared of what a big star I'm becoming, huh?

104
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:13,840
Not quite, Black Star.

105
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,440
It has nothing to do with you.

106
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:15,980
Huh?

107
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:21,840
The Perfect Boy.

108
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,120
Death the Kid's magnificent mission.

109
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:28,440
In the heart of the scorching Egyptian desert,

110
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,560
there is an ancient ruin.

111
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,860
It is known as the Pyramid of Anubis.

112
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:35,360
You will find a witch there, a necromancer.

113
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:37,480
She's raised a great number of the dead

114
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,800
who were entombed in the pyramid.

115
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:41,940
Every night, she leads out these mummies

116
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:43,580
to feed on human souls.

117
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,860
A necromancer is difficult to stop.

118
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,920
Her first set of mummies will be sent out

119
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,960
to create another set,

120
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:51,880
which will in turn create yet another

121
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:54,760
until she eventually has an entire army of mummies.

122
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:57,740
The ancient Pyramid of Anubis, I see.

123
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,040
It was built at a time when all construction

124
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,800
followed strict theories of symmetry.

125
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:03,160
Sounds great.

126
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:05,600
Actually, I was originally thinking about

127
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,640
assigning a three-star meister to this one.

128
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:08,820
Don't worry, Dad.

129
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,040
I can handle it myself.

130
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,600
After I've defeated the witch,

131
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,580
I can take some time to enjoy the architecture.

132
00:08:17,420 --> 00:08:19,460
So, what do you guys think?

133
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,760
Anyone else want to go find out

134
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:22,780
who took on the big mission?

135
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,580
Yeah, of course I do.

136
00:08:24,820 --> 00:08:26,680
Whoever this guy is, he's a real show-off.

137
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:28,060
He actually thinks he can build

138
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,520
a bigger reputation than mine.

139
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,140
Okay, then let's get going.

140
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:34,540
Hey, wait! Come back, you two!

141
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:35,040
Rocky!

142
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:57,540
Oh, would you just look at the exquisite symmetry?

143
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:03,440
All that time in weapon form

144
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:05,080
makes my back ache like crazy.

145
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:07,400
That thing's huge!

146
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,000
I could do without all this dust.

147
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:12,920
Let's all go inside, then, okay?

148
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,400
Are we sure that we want to do this?

149
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:16,580
This place gives me the crease.

150
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,760
It's okay. I'm sure we'll be fine.

151
00:09:18,820 --> 00:09:19,200
Let's go!

152
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:21,240
My eyes itch.

153
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:23,400
Wow.

154
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,720
It's perfect on the inside, too.

155
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:28,080
I hate it here.

156
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:30,780
I don't do well in creepy, dusty, icky places.

157
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,240
Hey, sis, I've been wondering something.

158
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:35,600
How come everyone always closes their eyes

159
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:36,300
when they sneeze?

160
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,300
Is it to keep their eyes

161
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:38,560
from popping out of their heads?

162
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,120
Do you know?

163
00:09:40,540 --> 00:09:41,520
I don't know, Patty.

164
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:42,620
That is certainly one theory

165
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,940
that might explain why it is.

166
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:45,220
Of course, it could also be

167
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,360
an involuntary reflex

168
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:47,880
triggered by normal brain activity.

169
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:48,760
Hmm.

170
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,740
Maybe I could do a test next time

171
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,460
I have a cold and tape my eyelids open.

172
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:54,640
Yes, but what if your theory is right

173
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:56,180
and your eyeballs do pop out of your head?

174
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,000
Okay, yeah.

175
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:58,440
You might be right there, big sis.

176
00:09:58,580 --> 00:09:59,680
You're so smart.

177
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,500
Kid, what's wrong with you?

178
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,700
You've been quiet for a long time now.

179
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:08,980
Well, uh, maybe it's my imagination,

180
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,740
but I have this horrible feeling

181
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:11,760
that the painting that I have

182
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,740
hanging in my living room

183
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:14,400
is leaning a little bit to the right.

184
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,840
Does that stop the painting

185
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:16,820
really matter right now?

186
00:10:16,820 --> 00:10:18,160
Yes, of course it matters.

187
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:19,220
What should I do?

188
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:20,960
I can't go on like this.

189
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:23,880
I can't wait.

190
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,300
I have to go back and make sure.

191
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,840
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

192
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,980
There's a limit to the insanity

193
00:10:29,980 --> 00:10:30,720
I'll put up with.

194
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:32,240
You can worry about it when we get home.

195
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,200
I'm worrying about it.

196
00:10:33,220 --> 00:10:33,940
I'm worrying about it.

197
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:34,740
Don't worry.

198
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:36,020
I won't let you worry about it.

199
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:36,480
I'm worrying.

200
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:37,100
I'm worrying.

201
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,060
Shut up!

202
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,500
You spoiled brat.

203
00:10:39,580 --> 00:10:39,980
I'm worrying.

204
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:40,440
I'm worrying.

205
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:40,520
I'm worrying.

206
00:10:43,700 --> 00:10:45,100
Oh, no, it's a mummy.

207
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:46,380
Mummy, mummy, mummy.

208
00:10:46,380 --> 00:10:46,440
Mummy!

209
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:55,840
Hey, they're kind of cute, aren't they?

210
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,100
Mummy, lick me!

211
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:02,940
Mummy, lick me!

212
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:03,860
Mummy, lick me!

213
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:05,740
Mummy, splatter!

214
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,100
How could this happen to me?

215
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,300
It's time to transform, Patty.

216
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:12,920
Okay.

217
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:14,800
Hey, kid, let's go.

218
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:18,240
Huh?

219
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,440
I don't know.

220
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:24,960
Dear Liz and Patty,

221
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:26,740
I'm still worrying about it.

222
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,060
Nothing you can say will help.

223
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,740
I'm going back home at once

224
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:30,660
to check on the painting.

225
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:31,780
Watch your step.

226
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:32,860
It's dark in the pyramid.

227
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:34,040
Death, the kid.

228
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:35,660
He's joking, right?

229
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:38,140
Patty!

230
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:38,800
Right!

231
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:47,920
Beat it, mummy!

232
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:56,800
Patty, don't stick me in that monster's dirty mouth!

233
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:57,120
Ew!

234
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,480
Okay, sorry!

235
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:13,380
Ancient statue, I lend you the dark heart from my body,

236
00:12:13,560 --> 00:12:15,900
that you may live again and do my bidding!

237
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:17,980
Awaken, pharaoh!

238
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,040
Your master is calling you!

239
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:27,340
The laugh of the pharaoh!

240
00:12:33,740 --> 00:12:35,180
He's got me!

241
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,180
I'm being dragged in!

242
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:39,020
He's going to eat my soul!

243
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:47,680
There is no one in this world

244
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,480
who can ever be my master.

245
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:51,260
All who enter,

246
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,720
beware the wrath of the pharaoh.

247
00:12:53,720 --> 00:13:04,420
Where do you suppose those two idiots

248
00:13:04,420 --> 00:13:05,420
have run off to now?

249
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:29,800
Ah, just my imagination, after all.

250
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:30,940
It's perfect.

251
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:34,720
And now, the girls are waiting for me to come back.

252
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,180
I should get going.

253
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,420
That's it.

254
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:41,000
We've recovered every last one of the mummy's souls.

255
00:13:43,740 --> 00:13:45,720
Do we have them all evenly split up?

256
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:46,600
Mm-hmm.

257
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:50,080
Since Kid would get all depressed if we didn't divide them up evenly.

258
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:55,140
I don't like this.

259
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:57,980
Did you hear that creepy noise coming from over that way?

260
00:13:58,880 --> 00:13:59,900
Let's just go.

261
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:01,720
Why don't we wait until Kid comes back?

262
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:03,620
Nah, it'll be okay.

263
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,520
I've got my big sis here with me.

264
00:14:07,080 --> 00:14:08,080
Oh, no.

265
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:12,780
The noise.

266
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,120
